Section 8. CPD Monitoring — Monitors shall be designated by the Board per region in the Philippines as recommended by the CPD Council for Pharmacists with the following qualifications and responsibilities:

8.1. Must be a licensed pharmacist with three (3) years of professional experience;

8.2. Must not be a member of the organizer/provider of the CPD program being monitored and duly certified by the CPD Council;

8.3. Must undergo training for CPD monitors provided by PRC or duly authorized trainers by the CPD Council;

8.4. Must submit prescribed reports to CPD Council through their secretary within fifteen (15) days after the program.

